# BigNumber

[Usage guidelines](https://pages.github.ibm.com/carbon/ibm-products/components/bignumber/usage/)

## Overview

BigNumber is used to display large values in a small area. The display of values
can be the value itself, or grouped in a `numerator/denominator` fashion. The
`fraction-digits` prop controls how many decimal places are shown, while the
`locale` prop controls number formatting conventions such as digit grouping and
decimal separators. Other optional props allow control over size, truncation, if
the value is a percentage as well as the addition of trending icon
functionality. The default locale is English(`en-US`) if one is not provided or
if the provided one is not supported.

[Supported locales](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/NumberFormat/NumberFormat#locales)

