# Step flows

## Table of Contents

- [Overview](#overview)
- [Example usage](#example-usage)

## Overview

The step flow utility can be used to compose stepping experiences across any
variation of components. This utility allows for stepping as commonly seen in
the `CreateTearsheet` and `CreateFullPage` patterns, but through a more
composable and headless delivery specifically built for use with web components.
This allows for the flexibility to incorporate stepped experiences within any
component.

Included assets:

- `StepInstance`
- `step-group`

## Getting started

Here's a quick example to get you started.

> **Note:** `StepInstance` is a
> [`ReactiveController`](https://lit.dev/docs/composition/controllers/). Pass
> `this` to the constructor so the controller can call `requestUpdate()` on your
> component whenever step state changes — no mixin required on your class.

### HTML

Basic usage example, initializes a `StepInstance` and accesses the step data via
`this._stepInfo.data`. Passing `this` to the constructor is what connects
mutations to your component's render cycle.

```ts
@customElement('my-stepped-component')
export class MySteppedComponent extends LitElement {
  // Pass `this` so mutations trigger requestUpdate() on this element.
  private _stepInfo = new StepInstance(this);

  connectedCallback() {
    super.connectedCallback();
    this._stepInfo.updateTotalStepCount = 3;
  }

  render() {
    const { totalSteps, currentStep } = this._stepInfo.data;
    return html`
      <cds-tearsheet
        class="step-tearsheet-with-util"
        selector-primary-focus="#tearsheet-story-text-input-a"
        ?open=${this._open}
        variant="wide"
        prevent-close-on-click-outside>
        <cds-tearsheet-body>
          <div slot="main-content">
            ${currentStep === 0 ? html`step 1` : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 1 ? html`step 2` : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 2 ? html`step 3` : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 3 ? html`step 4` : nothing}
          </div>
        </cds-tearsheet-body>
      </cds-tearsheet>
    `;
  }
}
```

Updating form state example, uses `StepInstance.updateFormState` to save form
state within the step instance. This allows for storing form data that can be
used in subsequent steps or when submitting.

```ts
@customElement('my-stepped-component')
export class MySteppedComponent extends LitElement {
  private _stepInfo = new StepInstance(this);

  connectedCallback() {
    super.connectedCallback();
    this._stepInfo.updateTotalStepCount = 3;
  }

  private _handleEmailInput(e: Event) {
    const savedFormState = structuredClone(
      this._stepInfo.data.formState
    ) as FormStateType;
    savedFormState.email = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    this._stepInfo.updateFormState = savedFormState;
  }

  render() {
    const { totalSteps, currentStep } = this._stepInfo.data;
    return html`
      <cds-tearsheet
        class="step-tearsheet-with-util"
        selector-primary-focus="#tearsheet-story-text-input-a"
        ?open=${this._open}
        variant="wide"
        prevent-close-on-click-outside>
        <cds-tearsheet-body>
          <div slot="main-content">
            ${currentStep === 0
              ? html` <cds-text-input
                  label="Email"
                  id="tearsheet-story-text-input-a"
                  value=${this._email}
                  @input="${this._handleEmailInput}"></cds-text-input>`
              : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 1 ? html`step 2` : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 2 ? html`step 3` : nothing}
            ${currentStep === 3 ? html`step 4` : nothing}
          </div>
        </cds-tearsheet-body>
      </cds-tearsheet>
    `;
